{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795539991,"nonce":"/SFC+Pm0/epJI9/uQutwFStUflI=","title":"jno.fem: building a boundary term re-tags the shared boundary Variables (right -\u003e gauss_right)","message":"Found on feat/fvm (Part B3). After one coupled solve whose jno.fem participant receives a boundary term (K1*fa + 5*(ua - ub) on its right edge), a second jno._coupling couple([...]) built from the SAME expressions finds the fem side bound to tag gauss_right instead of right (driver _analyse reads the Variables bound in the expression), and fails with: interface: the domain has no boundary facets tagged gauss_right. So the fem build of a boundary integral mutates the Variable objects of the user expression in place. Repro: the problems _fem_cold / _fvm_hot of tests/test_coupling_transient.py. Workaround: build fresh problems per coupling.\n\nCited as git-bug 44958ea in the commit history.","files":null}]}